<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00165</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9a95cb43-6241-4ba0-b834-62292fc7daf3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para class="os-raise-text-bold">Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 3 choose an equivalent equation.</para> 
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Which equation is equivalent to \(3x + 6 = 4x + 7\)?
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\( 9x=4x+7\)</item>
  <item> \(3x+18=4x+7\)</item>
  <item>\( 3x=4x+7\)</item>
  <item>\( 3x−1=4x\)</item>
  <item>\( 7x=1 \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>\(3x-1=4x\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Which equation is equivalent to \(3(x + 6) = 4x + 7\)?
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\( 9x=4x+7\)</item>
  <item> \(3x+18=4x+7\)</item>
  <item>\( 3x=4x+7\)</item>
  <item>\( 3x−1=4x\)</item>
  <item>\( 7x=1 \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>\(3x+18=4x+7\)</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Which equation is equivalent to \(4x + 3x = 7-6\)?
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\( 9x=4x+7\)</item>
  <item> \(3x+18=4x+7\)</item>
  <item>\( 3x=4x+7\)</item>
  <item>\( 3x−1=4x\)</item>
  <item>\( 7x=1 \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>\(7x=1\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    <emphasis>Select three </emphasis>equations that have 0 as a solution.
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(  2x+10=4x+10 \)</item>
  <item>\(5x + 7 = 0 \)</item>
  <item>\(3(x-2)=9\) </item>
  <item>\(2x-3+4x=4-7 \)</item>
  <item>\(4x=9x \)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>\(2x+10=4x+10\), \(4x=9x\), and \(2x-3+4x=4-7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which equation is equivalent to 6(x-3)=24?</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(  6x-3=24 \)</item>
  <item>\(x-3=4\)</item>
  <item>\(6x=21\)</item>
  <item>\(6x=27\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>\(x-3=4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Which of the following sets of equations are equivalent to each other?
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\)</item>
  <item>\(7(x+2)=21\) and \(7x +2=21\)</item>
  <item>\(5x - 2 = 7x +4\) and \(12x -2 =4\)</item>
  <item>\(6x-4=11\) and \(6x =7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>\(10(x+9) = 50\) and \(2(x+9)=10\). Each side of the equation was divided by 5. So the equations are equivalent.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Using the distributive property, choose which equation would be an equivalent equation to \(3(x-2) =7\).
  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(3x-2=7\)</item>
  <item>\(3x-6=7\)</item>
  <item>\(x-2=4\)</item>
  <item>\(3x=9\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>  
<para>3x - 6 =7. It is one of the solutions that could be equivalent to 3(x-2)=7</para></section>
</content>
